{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Strange Stories"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Fighting Among Animals"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe problems in social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le05ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Gerunds and Infinitives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> is a verb ending with -ing (doing).<br/>An <span class=\"strong\">infinitive</span> is to + verb (to do)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are some verbs that can only be followed by a gerund:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "consider (doing)<br/>practice (doing)<br/>dislike (doing)<br/>spend time (doing)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">Adult males <span class=\"strong\">dislike having</span> competition. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are some verbs that can only be followed by an infinitive:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "happen (to do)<br/>help (to do)<br/>want (to do)<br/>rend (to do)<br/>try (to do)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Fights <span class=\"strong\">tend to</span> be more like games than battles.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are some verbs that can be followed by an object plus an infinitive:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><br/>They <span class=\"strong\">challenge</span> other males <span class=\"strong\">to</span> fight for territory.<br/>It also <span class=\"strong\">helps</span> them <span class=\"strong\">to</span> recognize their kin.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If  you <span class=\"strong\">happened to</span> see two wild animals fighting, you would know it's an impressive sight. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Animals only <span class=\"strong\">want to</span> establish a hierarchy. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "He'll <span class=\"strong\">try to</span> win again when he is older."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You may even have <span class=\"strong\">considered asking</span> why animals of the same species fight."}, {"type": "example", "content": "All male animals, fight among themselves. Young males fight to <span class=\"strong\">practice fighting</span>. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional versus The Second Conditional "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the first conditional to talk about real situations in the the present of future.<br/><br/>You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "First conditional form:<br/>If + Simple Present verb, + will<br/><span class=\"italic\">If you come over, I'll help you with that.</span><br/>(you can come over)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Second conditional form:<br/>If + Simple Past verb,    + would<br/><span class=\"italic\">If you had time, I would help you with that.</span><br/>(I don't think or I know you don't have time)"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First Conditional<br/>(Cause and Effect)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second Conditional<br/>(Hypothetical Situations)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If they do this, they are also sure there is enough food for the herd.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If  you happened to see two wild animals fighting, you would know it's an impressive sight.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If the male is the strongest, he will be able to mate.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you spent time observing animals, you'd realize that fighting is the key to survival.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If his females have offspring, they will be strong, healthy, and have a of a chance of surviving.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If men behaved like animals, life among humans would be very different! </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember to use a comma (,) after the IF clause. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (I would = I'd)."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to die out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cease to live"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  more aggressive animals have survived, while the less aggressive have died out."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about animals"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "illogical"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "irrational"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It seems illogical."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "kin"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "of the same family "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It also helps them to recognize their kin, evaluate risk and cope with stressful situations."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "risk"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a dangerous chance"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It also helps them to recognize their kin, evaluate risk and cope with stressful situations."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cope"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to struggle or deal with something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It also helps them to recognize their kin, evaluate risk and cope with stressful situations."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "territory"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an area of land"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Adult males dislike having competition, so they challenge other males to fight for territory."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "newcomer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person or thing that has recently arrived"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Newcomers cannot expect to stay and eat."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hierarchy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "any system of persons, animals or things ranked one above another"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Animals only want to establish a hierarchy. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob03aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to tend"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have a tendency toward a particular quality"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content