ee all the animals. "}}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_8"}]}], "type": "TYP", "id": 10, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Let's see the animals ..."}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: <span class=\"bullet\">Listen to the audio.</span> <span class=\"bullet\">Type in the missing words. </span><span class=\"bullet\">Use capital letters where necessary. </span>"}]}]}, {"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}]}], "type": "RSLT", "id": 11, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "", "text": "<p>If  you happened to see two wild animals fighting, you would know it's an impressive sight. You may even have considered asking why animals of the same species fight. It seems illogical.</p><p>All male animals fight among themselves. Young males fight to practice fighting. It also helps them to recognize their kin, evaluate risk and cope with stressful situations.</p>", "id": 1}, {"time": "25000", "image": "", "text": "<p>Adult males dislike having competition, so they challenge other males to fight for territory. If they do this, they are also sure there is enough food for the herd. Newcomers cannot expect to stay and eat.</p> <p>If the male is the strongest, he will be able to mate. If his females have offspring, they will be strong, healthy, and have a of a chance of surviving.</p><p>If you've seen dogs fighting, you have noticed that the loser is not seriously hurt.  Animals only want to establish a hierarchy. Fights tend to be more like games than battles. If a male loses he's probably young. He lacks strength and experience. He'll try to win again when he is older.</p>", "id": 2}, {"time": "66500", "image": "", "text": "<p>For thousands of years the stronger, more aggressive animals have survived, while the less aggressive have died out. So, if you spend time observing animals, you'll realize that fighting is the key to survival.</p><p>There are important lessons to be learned from the animal world. Males of the same species fight, but none are killed. If men behaved like animals, life among humans would be very different!</p>", "id": 3}], "video_src": "engenn9le05ob03re2vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "video", "id": 2, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}]}]}